tate","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Florida State's first turquoise football uniforms are a tribute to Seminole Tribe","description":"Florida State's turquoise uniforms are a tribute to the Seminole Tribe of Florida.","published":"2026-11-16T01:03:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50495730/florida-state-football-turquoise-uniforms-seminole-tribe","type":"Story","byline":"Anthony Gharib","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Source: Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews out for season","description":"Mike Matthews sustained the injury during Tennessee's win Saturday at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-16T00:39:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50496356/tennessee-leading-receiver-mike-matthews-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma, boosted by crowd's ire at postponement, beats No. 19 Ole Miss","description":"The Oklahoma crowd let Ole Miss know what they thought of having their game delayed by a day, and the Sooners rode that energy to a 24-17 win over the Rebels.","published":"2026-11-16T00:22:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50495687/sooners-boosted-crowd-ire-postponement-beat-rebels","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football SP+ rankings for all 138 FBS teams","description":"The updated SP+ rankings, plus strength of schedule and résumé SP+, after this weekend's results.","published":"2026-11-15T22:56:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49868647/2026-college-football-sp+-rankings-all-138-fbs-teams","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sizing up college football's best races down the homestretch","description":"From spots in the CFP and SEC title game to the hunt for bowl eligibility, there's still a lot on the line.","published":"2026-11-15T22:17:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491637/connelly-college-football-best-races","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC fines Arkansas $500K for allowing fans to storm field vs. South Carolina","description":"The Southeastern Conference fined Arkansas $500,000 on Sunday for allowing fans to storm the field following a 34-6 victory over No. 17 South Carolina.","published":"2026-11-15T22:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493903/sec-fines-arkansas-500k-allowing-fans-storm-field-vs-south-carolina","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Tait Reynolds has torn meniscus, Christopher Vizzina a concussion","description":"Clemson lost starting QB Tait Reynolds for the rest of the season with a torn meniscus, while backup Christopher Vizzina has a concussion.","published":"2026-11-15T21:09:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493355/reynolds-torn-meniscus-vizzina-concussion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922988/jamari-johnson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson"},"pick":{"pick":24,"round":1,"team":"CIN","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jamari Johnson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:26Z","intro":"Jamari Johnson is an American college football tight end for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Louisville Cardinals.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Johnson attended Inglewood High School in Inglewood, California. He originally played quarterback before switching to tight end and also played wide receiver, running back and defensive end. As a senior, he was named the Ocean League MVP. Johnson was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to the University of Louisville to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Johnson played in five games and redshirted his first year at Louisville in 2023. He played in seven games as a redshirt freshman in 2024, recording 13 receptions for 158 yards and a touchdown, before suffering a season ending ankle injury. After the season, he entered the transfer portal and transferred to the University of Oregon. Johnson spent his first season at Oregon in 2025 as the backup to Kenyon Sadiq."}]}}